  "body": "## What changed\n\nThe gate's recording build (`debug build: <crate> (--no-run)`) now writes cargo's JSON to a file in the temporary directory. It does not use a pipe for it any more (`xtask/src/direct.rs`, `direct::cargo`).\n\n## Cause\n\n`direct::cargo` read the JSON through a pipe, in a reader thread. It joined that thread after cargo exited. A process that the build starts and that outlives the build inherits cargo's stdout. The sccache server is such a process: the first `rustc` wrapper call starts it when no server runs. That server keeps a copy of the write end of the pipe. The reader then got no end of file until the server stopped (its idle timeout). No watchdog runs during that join, because the watchdog stops when cargo exits. So the step waited after a green build. The wait depends on the sccache server state. The issue names a cargo \"rmeta handoff\". This worker did not see that wedge here. The pipe hold is the one wait of the prebuild path that depends on the sccache state, and the test below shows it.\n\nThe watchdog counts the file size (from the open handle) as output, as it counted the pipe bytes before. The gate reads the file when cargo exits and then deletes it. A descendant that holds the file cannot hold the gate. The decision record is `docs/decisions/3675-prebuild-json-file.md`.\n\n## Readings\n\n- Pinning test with the old `direct.rs`: FAILED, \"the step must end when cargo exits: 120.0331239s\". The 60 s watchdog did not fire.\n- Pinning test with the fix: pass, in less than 1 s.\n\n## Pinning test\n\n- `watchdog_tests::a_recording_build_ends_when_cargo_exits_not_when_its_descendants_do`: a fake cargo (the test executable, mode `orphan`) writes JSON and exits at once. Its descendant holds its stdout and sleeps 120 s. The step must end in less than 30 s, green, with the JSON.\n\n## Gate\n\n- `cargo test -p xtask --bin xtask`: 323 passed, 0 failed\n- `cargo clippy -p xtask --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean\n- Heavy lanes: none reached (xtask only).\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- A full batch gate run on this machine. The shared sccache server already ran, so a cold server start was not available without stopping the shared server. A second, private sccache server (other port) failed its compiles (\"connection was forcibly closed\"). So the cold-server path did not run end to end. The reported wedge (cargo 1.99.1) was not seen on this machine (cargo 1.100.0). The pipe hold is the probable cause, not a confirmed one. If the wedge comes back with this fix, reopen #3675.\n- `direct::record` still runs `cargo metadata` with a captured stdout. It builds nothing and was not changed.\n- Linux and macOS: the change uses only `std::fs` and `std::process`.\n\nProcess change: yes\nChangelog: none\nEffort: medium\n\nFixes #3675\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
